00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:01.910 align:start position:0%
 
good morning i'm kimberly god the  administrator for of deters employment  security division  this press briefing is held to provide  general information regarding leader esd  programs and processes  and is not specific to any one claim  please note that our press conference  process has changed as indicated in the  media advisory  we now are asking the media to provide  questions to dieter media  by wednesday each week so that we can  incorporate the information in our break  fees  as a reminder viewer cannot comment on  on  any current litigation with me today is  states chief economist dave schmidt he  will be providing  us the updated unemployment insurance  and pandemic unemployment assistance  data  thank you administrator god  standard unemployment insurance is for  nevadans who have lost their jobs  through no fault of their own  these people are these are people whose  employer pays taxes into the  unemployment insurance program through  the state's trust fund  and who both earned enough wages and  worked enough hours to be eligible for  those benefits  can we please put up the pie chart  as of july 18 2020 uh 590  92 700 total claims have been filed for  standard unemployment insurance  on the uinv site this number includes  both new claims  and reopened claims that have  intervening employment  also known as additional claims 571 048  of those claims have been filed  since march 14th of those eligible  filers who filed weekly claims for  in the week ending uh july 11th  uh 227 thousand two hundred and twenty  nine  or ninety percent of uh eligible claims  for that week were successfully paid  uh the number of weekly claims did  decline slightly from the prior week uh  was down by about five thousand  twelve thousand and 175 people filed for  benefits but were unemployed  employed and not eligible because they  had earnings for that week  that exceeded their weekly benefit  amount uh that's down slightly compared  to last week  1998 people had insufficient hours  and or wages to qualify for ui benefits  uh down by about 1 000 over the week  43 284 people did not file a claim for  the week  that's up slightly from last week and  has largely been steady over  the previous two months these are people  who started but  did not finish their weekly claim uh  never started their weekly claim  or reported to us that they were not  going to file a claim for the week  federal law does require that filers  file weekly claims  in order to receive payment uh finally  there were 23  411 other unp paid claims which was up  by about 6 000 from last week  these are filers whose claims are being  held because federal and state law  required deter to adjudicate their  claims  this number also includes claims that  have been identified as fraud  you can take the pie chart down pua is  pandemic unemployment assistance  and it's for those individuals  classified as contract 1099 and gig  workers  as well as other workers not covered  under traditional unemployment insurance  including people who have exhausted  their ui benefits  and all extended ui benefits  people still must be unemployed  underemployed unable to work or  unavailable for work  in a particular week due to covet 19.  to date nevada has taken uh 3149  uh pua initial claims uh as of july 20th  uh 300 873 of those have a weekly claim  filed or about 88 percent as of this  morning  121 980 claims have been paid  uh a total of uh over 1.3 billion  dollars  uh including both pua funds and fpuc  funds related to those pua claims  can we put up the table please  compared to nevada's estimated 82 000  self-employed workers  nevada has paid out over five thousand  one hundred dollars per self-employed  worker in regular pua benefits alone  uh that is the eighth highest level  among all states  uh by this measure and is uh includes  data through july 21st  uh you can take the table down  as of july 22nd uh dieter has paid out  nearly 5.4 billion dollars across all ui  and cares act  programs since the start of the pandemic  for comparison uh this exceeds the total  benefits paid out across both  unemployment insurance and all federal  extended benefits programs  uh in 2009 2010  and 2011 combined  uh with state unemployment benefits  remaining high uh the unemployment trust  fund continues to be drawn down  as of july 18th uh the trust fund  balance was uh 656.7 million dollars  which represents 5.8 weeks of benefit  benefit payments at current levels  uh in the event that the trust fund is  exhausted  the state would continue to pay  unemployment benefits  under the provisions of title 12 of the  social security act  uh and there will be no effect on  benefit payments uh just repeat  uh there will be no impact on benefit  payments  for unemployment insurance uh for those  eligible filers as a result of the  trust fund's decline  i we want to continue to remind  claimants in both ui and pua  that federal law requires you that you  must file a claim  every week in order to receive payment  for that week  many eligible claimants in both ui and  pua have not filed weekly claims and  therefore cannot be paid  with that will turn it back to  administrator gotham  thank you dave  um updates regarding quarter change um  this will  occur the first week in july and  requires states to check for new  and additional traditional ui  eligibility  peuc and seb or extended benefits  eligibility for the cares act and dol  guidance the coordination of programs  means that if you have traditional ui  or pandemic extended unemployment  eligibility or state extended benefit  eligibility you are required to file  for those benefits if you are eligible  before becoming eligible for pua  benefits pua filers receiving messaging  on their claim  indicating this new program eligibility  and traditional ui  peuc or seb should file their claim at  uinb.gov  using the claim itself portal  please go to employee to determine if  your claim reflects  this new eligibility please also visit  our website  dieter.nv.gov for further details  information and guidance  updates regarding um the federal  pandemic unemployment compensation  ending this week currently the carers  act federal pandemic unemployment  compensation  also known as fpec dollars commonly  referred to as the traditional 600  dollars added eligibility for ui  sunsets this saturday july 25th  this means that starting for the week  beginning sunday july 26th  filers are scheduled to receive their  calculated weekly benefit amount going  forward  dieter has been in communications with  the department of labor governor's  office and  federal delegates and we currently have  no updated information  on any extensions at this time filers  who are  eligible during the period that f-puck  was available  will still be able to receive f-puc  benefits for all eligible weeks  please watch for additional updates on  our website and dieter.nv.gov  as this information may change with the  pending legislation being considered by  congress  questions about pua function system  functionality  we have received questions for filers  regarding why it takes a number of days  or dates change  to receive payments on pua benefits  once it is reflected in the system that  the payments have issued  this is due to process steps required to  review payments to ensure  accurate disbursement of funds we are  aware that this is frustrating for  filers as you wait for these funds to  become available  we continue to work with our vendor to  automate this process and make it more  efficient  we also received inquiries from ui and  pua filers regarding decline  transactions for their ui and  pua banking accounts cards if you have  specific transactions declined  please check with your banking  institution for details  for filers that receive notice that an  account has been suspended or frozen  please call the ui call center or the  pool call center for further  instructions  you will have to provide identity  information so be prepared with this  information  requests for information regarding  overpayments  ui filers advised of an overpayment of  benefits must contact our call center  for updated information on ways to pay  back this money  for filers and current weekly filing  status you may see an offset  of continu current and future weeks of  benefits  in accordance with ui law and guidance  updates regarding pua appeals we  continue to receive questions regarding  appeals functionality  this functionality is operational whoa  filers are able to file an appeal  request through employee nv  filers wishing to file an appeal may do  so at employee through your account  portal  appeals requests for previously issued  eligibility determinations  will be honored for 30 calendar days  from july 18th  you may also contact the call center for  further instructions on how to file your  appeal  filers will need to watch for  communication in their portal in august  after filing their appeals request  information about access to the call  centers  dieter continues to work for ways to  provide additional resources to address  every claim  we continue to work with our call center  staff to update processes  and provide customer service feedback to  the best to best serve the data filers  we recommend choosing our offered  callback features to minimize time  waiting on the phone we continue to work  with the governor's office and our  legislators  and our federal delegations on funding  and staffing resources to provide and  expand service delivery for every  nevadan  deter is also experiencing difficulties  contacting filers as part of the  adjudication process  our staff may be calling you from the  following phone numbers  so please work with your carriers to  unblock these numbers  775-687-7101  702-486 is  and 702-486-3387  please ensure that you enable these  numbers with your mobile or telephone  carrier so you don't miss our calls  we will provide those phone numbers  again after the press briefing  additional additionally many employers  are seeking filers  who may be seeking job placement  assistance our job  is remain closed for the in-person  assistance  however our virtual job placement  services are available at employment  please visit employee nb for up-to-date  job placement opportunities  we've received a lot a number of  questions about system  security and fraud we strongly advise  nevadans use guidance from dieter as a  trusted source of information  there is no cost to file a claim online  and persons offering to complete or  assist with claims for fees  or to access your personal information  is not authorized by dieter  dieter has heard from many businesses  and citizens that may have had their  personal identifying information  accessed without their consent and used  for  filing for fraudulent claims this is not  a result of  any known data breach within dieter  deter actively monitors its systems  and works with reputable companies and  its vendors to ensure that all data is  maintained securely  nevada is actively working with law  enforcement entities and the department  of labor to detect  prevent and address fraud this includes  participation by dieter  as a member of the attorney general's  coven 19 fraud task force  if you believe that a claim has been  filed fraudulently using your  information  or you know somebody is committing fraud  the quickest way to report this  information  is three ways through deters updated  online fraud form at deter.nb.gov  select fraud reporting form under quick  links  or through the fbi's internet crime  complaint center  known as ic3 at www.ic3.gov  employers needing to report fraudulent  filings can respond to filing notices  indicating they believe the claim is  fraudulent  note the action to take action taken to  resolve these reports  may or may not include contact from our  office  tips on how to protect your personal  information can be found on our  website bulletin board dieter.nv.gov  excuse me note that unemployment fraud  is considered a felony under nevada  revised statute  nevada will be following fraudulent  claims up to and including prosecution  and other civil remedies afforded under  law we will be limiting further  information related to any  investigations and will not be sharing  details to protect the case integrity  thank you and we will look forward to  speaking with you again next friday with  additional updates and information  this concludes our remarks for today's  briefing

